他再次尝试。
he tries again.

677
00:40:30,970 --> 00:40:35,060
这一次，他快速的在一张图像中无错误地
He now quickly identifies five enemy targets

678
00:40:35,180 --> 00:40:39,340
识别出了5个敌方目标。
in one image without making a single mistake.

679
00:40:39,450 --> 00:40:42,010
脑部经过刺激后的人们，
In the people who got brain stimulation,

680
00:40:42,120 --> 00:40:45,980
每个人在一个小时的训练之后
every individual was performing at expert level

681
00:40:46,090 --> 00:40:48,710
都表现出了专家水平。
after an hour of training.

682
00:40:48,820 --> 00:40:51,580
平均来说，使用TDCS刺激的学员
On average, novices who've had TDCS

683
00:40:51,690 --> 00:40:56,820
比起未经刺激的识别率要高出两倍。
identify twice as many targets compared with those who haven't.

684
00:40:56,930 --> 00:40:59,420
当他把受试者放回脑部扫描仪中，
When he put subjects back in the scanner,

685
00:40:59,540 --> 00:41:00,660
Michael发现
Michael discovered

686
00:41:00,770 --> 00:41:03,390
他们脑部的活跃模式
that the patterns of activity in their brains

687
00:41:03,510 --> 00:41:05,530
永久的改变了。
are permanently changed.

688
00:41:05,640 --> 00:41:09,270
他们新获得的能力即使在刺激撤除后
Their newly acquired skills stay with them

689
00:41:09,380 --> 00:41:12,040
也长期伴随着他们。
even after the stimulation wears off.

690
00:41:13,450 --> 00:41:16,970
不难想象这种技术的日后应用，
It's not hard to imagine where this technology could end up.

691
00:41:17,090 --> 00:41:19,910
大学的孩子们可以用它来增强计算能力，
College kids could use it for calculus,

692
00:41:20,020 --> 00:41:23,410
虎妈(要求非常严格的母亲)让孩子进行的完美钢琴演奏会，
tiger moms for pitch-perfect piano recitals.

693
00:41:23,530 --> 00:41:25,780
这些都只需要分离出脑部
Just isolate the part of the brain

694
00:41:25,900 --> 00:41:27,750
你需要学习该技能的部分，
you need to learn a skill,

695
00:41:27,860 --> 00:41:31,520
使用TDCS帽能够让你在几分钟内成为大师。
and a TDCS cap could make you a master in minutes.

696
00:41:32,630 --> 00:41:33,520
啊！
Whee!

697
00:41:33,640 --> 00:41:38,430
我用TDCS刺激了许多许多次脑部，
I've stimulated my brain with TDCS many, many times.

698
00:41:38,540 --> 00:41:41,030
我发现这样可以让我集中注意力，
I've noticed this intense focus

699
00:41:41,140 --> 00:41:42,870
非常仔细的集中于
and the ability to concentrate very carefully

700
00:41:42,980 --> 00:41:46,900
我正审阅的材料上。
on material that I'm looking at.

701
00:41:47,020 --> 00:41:49,040
我认为这会让我们大大受益，
And I think it would be a great benefit

702
00:41:49,150 --> 00:41:51,370
神经科学的工具
to be able to use the tools of neuroscience

703
00:41:51,490 --> 00:41:53,310
能让人类受益，
to benefit people,

704
00:41:53,420 --> 00:41:58,850
让人们高水平表现自己。
to make sure that they could perform at a high level.

705
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:02,750
随着我们对脑部活跃区域
As we learn more and more

706
00:42:02,870 --> 00:42:07,220
越来越多的了解，
about which structures in the brain are being activated,

707
00:42:07,340 --> 00:42:09,390
我们能表明持续运作的是你的一部分(潜意识)，
we can show it's part of you going on,

708
00:42:09,510 --> 00:42:11,710
无论你是否在思考。
whether you're thinking about it or not.

709
00:42:13,510 --> 00:42:15,730
我们做的很多事都是无意识的--
Much of what we do is unconscious --

710
00:42:15,840 --> 00:42:18,070
我们的喜好、偏见。
our preferences, our prejudices.

711
00:42:18,180 --> 00:42:20,040
就像有人回来主持这场表演，
Someone back there is guiding the show.

712
00:42:20,150 --> 00:42:21,240
那谁才是管事的呢？
Who's in charge?

713
00:42:21,350 --> 00:42:24,790
我认为是无意识的思维才是管事的。
And I think it's the unconscious that's in charge.

714
00:42:29,490 --> 00:42:33,950
科学已经证实我们的确有两种思维。
Science has proven that we really do have two minds.

715
00:42:34,060 --> 00:42:37,190
一种驱动着意识思维。
One drives our conscious thoughts.

716
00:42:37,300 --> 00:42:42,390
另一种隐藏在脑后没日没夜的工作，
The other is a shadow brain that never stops working.

717
00:42:42,500 --> 00:42:46,760
它保护我们不受伤害，还能治疗我们的身体，
It protects us from harm, heals our bodies,

718
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:50,570
让我们想得更快，更具有创造力。
allows us to think faster and more creatively.

719
00:42:50,680 --> 00:42:54,500
我们已经打开了潜意识的一些秘密，
We've unlocked some secrets of the subconscious.

720
00:42:54,620 --> 00:42:58,410
当我们把这种隐藏的力量全部解锁时，
When we finally tap into its hidden powers,

721
00:42:58,520 --> 00:43:00,760
我们能实现什么样的成就呢？
who knows what we will achieve?

